# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in the keys. They are read only
# by the Vite dev/preview server (see vite.config.ts), which proxies the
# `/api/*` routes to the upstream APIs with the keys attached. `vite build`
# never reads this file, so no key is ever part of the built site.

# val_scraper -> HenrikDev Valorant API (key required)
# Get a free Basic key: https://api.henrikdev.xyz/dashboard/ -> API Keys -> Generate New Key
HENRIKDEV_API_KEY=

# mr_scraper -> rivalsmeta.com's JSON API (no key needed). Nothing to set.

# Optional: point a local proxy at a different upstream (e.g. a mock server).
# HENRIKDEV_API_BASE=https://api.henrikdev.xyz
# MARVELRIVALS_API_BASE=https://rivalsmeta.com/api      # or https://api.rivalstracker.com/api (same data)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION (Cloudflare Pages)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT use this file. Set the variable on the Cloudflare project instead:
#   Workers & Pages -> <project> -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets -> Add
#     Type: Secret, Name: HENRIKDEV_API_KEY, Environment: Production (and Preview if wanted)
# or with Wrangler:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put HENRIKDEV_API_KEY --project-name <project>
# Then redeploy. The Pages Functions in functions/api/* read it at runtime.
# The mr_scraper proxy needs no variables.
